<title>ITALY: Italy's Florence sees June CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Florence sees June CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>FLORENCE, Italy 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Florence said its June consumer price index stood at 0.0 percent month-on-month and 1.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In May, Florence's inflation rate was 0.4 percent and 1.5 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Florence is one of 11 Italian cities to publish CPI data on Friday and Monday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.08 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to May 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0    (0.4)    1.2    (1.5)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.3    (0.3)   -1.2   (-0.5)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.1   (-0.2)    1.8    (1.8)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.0   (-0.1)    3.6    (3.5)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.1    (1.0)    2.4    (2.4)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.6    (0.0)    2.6    (2.0)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.2    (0.2)    1.1    (1.0)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -2.4    (0.1)   -3.7   (-1.3)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.0)    4.5    (4.5)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0    (0.7)    3.2    (3.5)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.2    (1.6)    2.6    (2.9)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
